# Queue UI-CMS Connection (Skeletal Foundation)

## Scope
Verify complete flow: UI requests → Queue → process one at a time → CMS → CMS response → Queue verify and pop → Queue response back to UI. If this doesn't work, all other concerns are irrelevant.

## Out of Scope
Priority queues, idempotency, retry logic, circuit breaker, concurrency control, fingerprinting - all advanced features. Only basic flow verification.

# Aftermath target
After completion: UI can send basket reservation request to queue, queue processes it one at a time, CMS receives and processes, response verified, queue pops job, response returned to UI. Full end-to-end flow working with human-observable console logs.

## Definition of Done
[ ] UI→Queue connection: basket reservation requests stream from UI to queue
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Request received from UI', { requestId, type })` on enqueue
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Job added to queue', { stream, jobId })` after XADD
    [ ] Test: Send request from UI, verify job appears in Redis stream
[ ] Queue→CMS connection: process one at a time, feed to CMS
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Processing job', { jobId, requestId })` when job dequeued
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Sending to CMS', { requestId, payload })` before CMS call
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: CMS response received', { requestId, success })` after CMS returns
    [ ] Test: Enqueue 3 jobs, verify logs show sequential processing (job 1 complete before job 2 starts)
[ ] CMS→Queue connection: verify response and pop
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Verifying CMS response', { requestId, success })` before pop
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Job popped from queue', { jobId, requestId })` after XACK
    [ ] Test: Process job, verify job removed from pending entries
[ ] Queue→UI connection: response pass back to UI
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Response sent to UI', { requestId, result })` before return
    [ ] Test: Send request from UI, verify UI receives response
[ ] Stock formula: available = stock - reservedStock
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Stock calculation', { stock, reservedStock, available })` on CMS update
    [ ] Test: Reserve stock, verify available = stock - reservedStock
